'' A static whose initialiser is an ADDRESS written into an INTEGER slot emits a
'' ptrtoint constant expression; the pointer-typed spelling beside it is a bare symbol.
'' The comparisons are differenced against fbc -- the ADDRESSES themselves differ
'' between the two builds, which is why the test prints whether they match and not what
'' they are.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/static-addr-init.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/static-addr-init.out
